  "newFindings": [
    "43A byte5FF has a proved negative role in native HEV telemetry policy, not a per-cell fault/invalid meaning and not a qualifiedSOC reading.",
    "BMS policy codes have explicit native reason strings for disabled collection paths. They are not battery-health states.",
    "Count-source validity differs by entry path: sync range/marker gate, raw43A byte gate and later callback signed upper bound are not equivalent.",
    "HAL count filterFF updates scalar cache255 before returning2; these type0 updates suppress the new callback through duplicate suppression. A retained native array count can therefore disagree with a new invalid scalar cache.",
    "Native array buffers begin as zeros. A count-complete latch can coexist with uncopied zero slots after duplicate pages; no array-value read alone distinguishes those zeros from transmitted zeros.",
    "Human-readable charging/fault and discharge-main-contactor labels exist on separate34400018/34400010 APIs. The traced array paths do not attach those labels to a cell/probe code."
  ],
